      'Client date: 2026-11-14. **Exact full/light geolocation compatibility is now verified. The exact file also verifies the native fire-mask class meanings. The algorithm-QA and physical response/registration gaps remain unresolved, so none of the sixteen candidates becomes qualified. G4: ADJUSTMENT_WITHHELD.**','',
      '## Actual answer','',
      'The preserved VNP14 file explicitly names the full VNP03MOD granule as its geolocation input. The acquired MODLL companion names that same full input. All latitude, longitude and height values agree across the entire paired swaths: **10,393,600 values per variable, 31,180,800 total, zero stored differences**. This includes native fill values; it does not imply that every pixel is a valid observation. Replacing full MOD coordinates with this MODLL cannot change the sixteen candidate locations. It does not prove absolute ground-location accuracy.','',
      'The VNP14.002 fire-mask variable contains an embedded ten-class legend applicable to the exact acquired production. Class 5 is natively non-fire land; class 3 is non-fire water; class 1 is trimmed. This resolves native class interpretation without borrowing a Collection 1 guide. The separate algorithm-QA variable declares only a bit field. No authoritative bit-definition applicability statement for SP NPP_PR14 1.6.1 / PGE 2.0.4 was obtained. Raw QA word 2 is retained without a borrowed decoder.','',
