      'B0 remains unchanged. B1 common support is withheld. B2 has stronger provenance/geolocation and native-class interpretation but no qualified physical pairing. B3 Aqua/750 m remains unqualified. B4 combined historical estimand is not released. No model or new fit preregistration is justified on this one enriched pass. The inherited minimum of 30 qualified passes across five independent 7-day blocks is unmet and is not itself a power guarantee.','',
      'Original `reports/G4_DECISION.md` is byte-preserved. It still requires qualified paired support, complete metadata-qualified training/holdout inventory, sealed geographic/temporal evaluation, practical-effect and bias/rank/sensitivity guardrails, independent ICNF/CAL FIRE corroboration, dependence-aware intervals and science-owner/independent-human signoff. Portugal/California and Canada-2024 holdouts remain sealed and unevaluated. G4: ADJUSTMENT_WITHHELD.','',
      '## Implemented application behavior','',
      'Open `http://127.0.0.1:5174/?region=canada&study=phase10`. After hash-bound acceptance, the first screen is the June 13, 2023 L2 experiment with F01 centered automatically. It shows the observed 375 m signal, candidate coarse class, qualification status, scientific result and limit. Three named source-center labels, colored native markers and candidate-association lines are visible; no fabricated footprint polygon is drawn. Context/detail zoom preserves the selection.','',
      'The new experiment calendar explicitly reports native L2 positive-mask totals for this AOI/pass, separate from historical FIRMS monthly totals. Native count cards and historical period controls are hidden during the experiment. The existing Phase 9 panel also synchronizes its background map to June 2023 rather than leaving June 2010 behind it. Returning to native history preserves the earlier source/filter/date/cell query and camera; historical navigation is not overwritten with June 2023.','',
      'Evidence Passport now describes the selected experiment, not unrelated native monthly counts. It contains UTC scan bounds, the actual NASA FP_day acquisition flag (all sixteen are Night), version-specific QA matrix, exact full/light identities, original six source hashes, new geolocation/qualification hashes and direct artifact exports. Light/dark cartography remains a visual theme. Selected three-source CSV retains baseline fields and appends qualification identity/status hashes.','',
